; ---- PASS 4.1 · THE CUT WITNESS -------------------------------------------
;
; The blade's line is fixed in SCREEN space: it runs through the centre of the
; frame at -30 degrees, whatever is in front of the camera. So the only question
; staged here is WHAT IS IN FRONT OF IT, and on PASS 4 the measured answer was:
;
;     42% of the line, no geometry at all (sky)
;     36% of it, a FLAT FACE square-on to the eye (ndot 0.84-1.00)
;     21% of it, a silhouette the eye could measure a step against
;
; — including six unbroken samples of dead-flat wall running straight through
; the centre of the picture. A displacement is only legible where something
; already has an EDGE: move a flat featureless face by 15px and the frame is
; pixel-identical. `tools/probe_iaido_line.gd` prints that breakdown, and it is
; the reason 世界 A/B 的错位仍然太含蓄 was never a `separation_px` problem.
;
; This is one dressed ruin column, placed so the line crosses BOTH of its
; vertical edges — 一根原本连续的直线被错开 8-14px, in the middle of the frame,
; on an element that has no other business in the shot. It is inert scenery: it
; is not part of the cut, it has no script, and it casts a shadow because a
; column standing on the deck that does not would read as floating.
[sub_resource type="BoxMesh" id="CutWitnessMesh"]
size = Vector3(0.45, 4.5, 0.45)

[sub_resource type="StandardMaterial3D" id="CutWitnessMaterial"]
albedo_color = Color(0.255, 0.245, 0.225, 1)
roughness = 0.92
metallic = 0.0

