; MOVED BACK, AND THE ENEMY IS WHY. At z=-4 this block's footprint covered the
; target: the dummy at x=-2.45 sat with its left 0.85m INSIDE a 5x1.5x5 box and
; its lower 1.25m inside the block's height, so from the camera — which is to
; the right of the block — only the sliver of the body poking out past the
; block's right face was ever on screen. Measured on the PASS 4 hero hold, the
; target's visible width was 86px against the 138px its own radius projects to,
; and what did show shared the block's exact luminance band.
;
; 身体还埋在建筑里 is not a lighting problem and it is not a separation problem.
; Pushed to z=-8.5 the block stops occluding anything, stays the dark mass on
; the left of the shot, and becomes the BACKDROP the target needs to be read
; against — a body cannot be seen to be cut in half against nothing.
[node name="RaisedPlatform" type="StaticBody3D" parent="."]
position = Vector3(-5, 0.75, -8.5)

[node name="MeshInstance3D" type="MeshInstance3D" parent="RaisedPlatform"]
mesh = SubResource("PlatformMesh")

[node name="CollisionShape3D" type="CollisionShape3D" parent="RaisedPlatform"]
shape = SubResource("PlatformShape")

[node name="Player" parent="." instance=ExtResource("1")]

; ON THE BLADE'S LINE, AND CLOSER. The plane is cut from the camera, so its
; normal has no z component: a body keeps its exact relationship to the wound
; when it is moved along z, which is what lets the target be brought forward
; without re-deriving anything. x=-2.487 puts the wound at world y=1.00 — 0.75m
; up the body, i.e. the middle of the cylinder rather than a shave off its top.
; z=-1.8 takes it from 8.6m to 6.8m, which is 174px -> 232px of body at 720p
; and 0.93 -> 1.10 px per centimetre: a 2-4cm misalignment goes 1.9-3.7px
; -> 2.2-4.4px, and the 10-20cm release goes 9-19px -> 11-22px.
[node name="TechnicalDummy" parent="." instance=ExtResource("2")]
position = Vector3(-2.487, 0.25, -2.6)

